      "worked_solution": "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/c0c348883f19c18a48444415da35aeaa27f8a18606bf5955e34aec416e248cad.svg) be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) be the region bounded by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/278f99df1e14fe0ebfb61bdb72262a62670dcaa60d322148bc3ee591b278ec2d.svg) If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/1aaddf0d4be4d873ff6c0600b0b239e0565a05ca8daaff7ca92bd5c70bebcf03.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/4be111afe7c23428ae5024a8bb9424de4d5b9e8cce74d2258fdffb9bdca9bcfd.svg) have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/87e7e0743ecd6609730f4b9a9b3681b1f360ca86bcb209e03561a197b18782f3.svg) then Green's theorem states that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/accf185e064f4c9c99cc6ad1437aabc7d5471cc332ff6c38d51a3f11ec6e26f2.svg)\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/090c7fe781ec77412a904bb44dda28812c8a4e9a8524886e36041ffcabe9f0a4.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/d719ec6c4bb88290d50d81fc268cc438cb3002659b6ac79210889d779a09d44c.svg) So,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/94e9af3cff89c9bcf412776abcab67d1852ba083401829edcd746cb19311c8b9.svg)\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/ec5ca2469ae1fd23385b27e906cb952f6b07c2bbfe02acbc42afa20284d4a122.svg)",
